  "note": "F4-S5 QA fixture (premium computation + thin-cohort fallback). PRE-SHAPED, same convention as ws1-anchor-drift.json. fetched_at is deliberately in the past (owner ruling 1). Every sqft is 1000 so psf == initial_ask/1000 and every expected median is readable by eye. Five deliberately-shaped cohorts: 2025 carries FIVE comps at psf 1..5 so the min_cohort_size boundary can be walked below/at/above 4 by toggling weights alone (5 selected -> median 3.0 - 4 selected -> 2.0 - 3 selected -> fallback to the pulled five -> 3.0, a value no selected-only computation produces); 2024 carries three comps so an EXCLUDED comp's presence in the fallback set is decisive (fallback 2.0 vs selected-only 1.0); 2023 carries the same three with the psf-3.00 comp ~6.9mi away so a FILTERED comp's presence in the fallback set is decisive under max_distance_mi; 2022 carries a missing-sqft comp whose initial_ask (10000) is far off the cohort so any leak into a median is loud; 2021 carries exactly ONE comp - the structurally-zero-premium case (QUEUE row 11a), pinned here only for the flags that must accompany it, never for the premium value itself. See backend/tests/api/test_f4s5_premium_basis.py for the worked values. ROW 10B: every comp also states first_listed -- the stitched start date real shaping always sets (pipeline/shape.py::_build_comp) and the date removed_on, and therefore DerivedComp.days_since_removal, is measured from. Without it a removed comp went over the wire carrying a removal rung beside a null count, i.e. the row 'removed nulld -- classifying', while responses.py declares that field null IFF removal_class is null. first_listed is not free: cohort_year is its year, removed_on is it plus effective_dom, and the removal rung is the ladder applied to as_of minus removed_on -- so the pre-shaped format lets an author state one fact four times, which is how they drifted apart. backend/tests/unit/test_r10b_preshaped_pulls_are_shapeable.py re-ties them, over this directory's listing rather than a fixed list of filenames, so a new pre-shaped pull is covered the day it is added. All fifteen comps' stated rungs and cohort years already agreed with a real start date, so nothing else here changed -- every worked premium value in test_f4s5_premium_basis.py is untouched.",
